summary:
  The cleanup a panel runs when it starts takes no address file an earlier
  session left behind.

history:
  With a file for each recording, a panel that dies between a write and its
  capture leaves a file holding a station's address, and nothing of the next
  session would ever name it again. The first cleanup takes every file whose
  name carries a start time before this session began.

target:
  package/contents/ui/RecordingEngine.qml

find:
              + RecLogic.olderFilesLine(PodcastLogic.shQuote(_recUrlBase + "-"), _recBornMs)

replace:
              + RecLogic.olderFilesLine(PodcastLogic.shQuote(_recUrlBase + "-"), 0)

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_recordingengine.qml::test_the_start_of_the_panel_takes_what_older_sessions_left
  and tests/test_recording_stop_race.py::test_the_start_of_the_panel_takes_what_older_sessions_left.
  Line-neutral.
